# 02 - Create DataFrame (All Ways) (PySpark Practical)

This practical covers creating DataFrames using:
- list of tuples
- list of dicts
- schema (manual)
- RDD
- file (CSV/JSON/Parquet)
- range()

---

## 0) Setup SparkSession

```python
from pyspark.sql import SparkSession

spark = SparkSession.builder     .appName("CreateDataFrameAllWays")     .master("local[*]")     .getOrCreate()
```

---

## 1) Create DataFrame using List of Tuples (Most Common)

```python
data = [
    (1, "Pramod", "IT", 50000),
    (2, "Akash", "HR", 60000),
    (3, "Rahul", "IT", 45000)
]

df = spark.createDataFrame(data, ["id", "name", "dept", "salary"])
df.show()
```

---

## 2) Create DataFrame using List of Dicts

```python
data_dict = [
    {"id": 1, "name": "Pramod", "dept": "IT", "salary": 50000},
    {"id": 2, "name": "Akash", "dept": "HR", "salary": 60000},
    {"id": 3, "name": "Rahul", "dept": "IT", "salary": 45000},
]

df2 = spark.createDataFrame(data_dict)
df2.show()
```

---

## 3) Create DataFrame with Manual Schema (Best Practice)

Why manual schema?
- avoids wrong inference
- avoids performance issues
- ensures correct types

```python
from pyspark.sql.types import StructType, StructField, IntegerType, StringType

schema = StructType([
    StructField("id", IntegerType(), True),
    StructField("name", StringType(), True),
    StructField("dept", StringType(), True),
    StructField("salary", IntegerType(), True)
])

df3 = spark.createDataFrame(data, schema=schema)
df3.printSchema()
df3.show()
```

---

## 4) Create DataFrame from RDD (Interview Topic)

```python
rdd = spark.sparkContext.parallelize(data)
df4 = spark.createDataFrame(rdd, ["id", "name", "dept", "salary"])
df4.show()
```

---

## 5) Create DataFrame using spark.range()

This is useful for generating sample data quickly.

```python
df_range = spark.range(1, 11)  # 1 to 10
df_range.show()
```

---

## 6) Create DataFrame from Files (Quick Demo)

### 6.1 CSV
```python
df_csv = spark.read.option("header", "true").csv("data/employees.csv")
```

### 6.2 JSON
```python
df_json = spark.read.json("data/employees.json")
```

### 6.3 Parquet
```python
df_parquet = spark.read.parquet("data/employees.parquet")
```

---

## 7) Summary

- Most common = list of tuples + column names
- Best practice = manual schema using StructType
- RDD creation is mostly interview only
- spark.range() is great for quick test data
- Reading from files is real-world ingestion

